dialect protocol
protocol stdio.xlsx.diff
version 1
schema stdio.xlsx
start record

# FG-wave: REAL binary diff frame, replacing F6's `print_diff().into_bytes()` text-as-binary
# shortcut (`../../🦀️.rs`'s old `DiffCodec::encode_diff`/`decode_diff`) -- per this
# ticket's own `📖️grammar-recipe.md` §4/§6 census, 100% of stdio's `DiffCodec` impls were still on
# this shortcut before this pilot ladder; confirmed live (not assumed) by direct read of this
# artifact's own file before this wave. `format u8` + `flags u8` (bit0 = `opc` present, bit1 =
# `workbook` present -- `XlsxDiff` has exactly these TWO independently-optional top-level fields)
# as two REAL fixed fields, individually protocol-walked -- same shape docx's own
# `🔺️diff/💾️binary/📡️.protocol.semio` (this wave's OPC pattern-setter) establishes.
#
# Past that header, `opc`/`workbook` (whichever `flags` marks present, in that FIXED order) are
# bundled into ONE opaque trailing `bytes` chain: `XlsxOpcDiff`/`XlsxWorkbookDiff` both recurse
# into genuinely data-carrying, recursive-shaped structures (`XlsxCellValue`'s `Formula.cached`
# self-nests; the shared `NamedTripleDiff<K,D,T>` collection triple has no `Prim`-describable
# generic shape) -- the SAME `protocol-prim-ref-recursion` mechanism gap every other stdio
# artifact's diff payload hits (`Prim::Ref` unconditionally errors in `walk_protocol`, confirmed
# unchanged through every pilot, `📖️grammar-recipe.md` §5). This dialect's `Cond` also cannot test
# an individual FLAG BIT (only a field's whole value against a literal), so a per-bit-guarded
# field list isn't expressible even before the recursion is considered -- bundling both fields
# into one opaque tail, rather than partially structuring only the non-recursive-looking one, is
# the honest, minimal-surface choice, same reasoning docx's own file documents.
#
# The Rust `encode_diff`/`decode_diff` side stays genuinely, fully structured past this header --
# real LEB128-varint-framed length-prefixed strings/bytes, 1-byte tri-state presence tags, and
# 1-byte enum-variant tags for `XlsxCellValue`'s six variants (`N`/`S`/`I`/`B`/`F`/`E`), plus
# generic named-triple binary codecs reused across all six `NamedTripleDiff<K,D,T>` instantiations
# this artifact's diff carries (see `../../🦀️.rs`'s own `BinaryCodecs` region) --
# round-trip tested independently of this protocol description, same honest-boundary treatment
# `📖️grammar-recipe.md` §2.5 documents.
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field flags u8
chain payload bytes
